The clean LLVM bridge check also passes independently: 212 finite cases generated from the trusted canonical oracle were translated with the trusted front end and executed against the freshly built supplied semantics; `krun` exited 0 with `.K`, `NoExc`, and exit cell 0. I’m writing the final review now. The remaining limitations are explicit trust boundaries—not proof shortcuts—so the anticipated classification is legitimate with concerns rather than a failure.
